aper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.prop-2adic-nogo"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.prop-2adic-nogo"],"id":"long.prop-2adic-nogo","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Proposition 10.4 (Centred completion of fixed-precision 2-adic data)","locator":"Long record Proposition 10.4, p. 114, label prop:2adic-nogo","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Fix $u\\ge1$ and a finite list $(v_i,a_i)_{0\\le i<m}$, where $v_i\\ge0$ are integers and the integers $a_i$ are odd. For every initial integer $e_0$, there are integers $z_i,e_{i+1}$ such that\n$$\ne_{i+1}=2e_i+2^{v_i}(a_i+2^u z_i),\\qquad\n |e_{i+1}|\\le2^{v_i+u-1}\\qquad(0\\le i<m).\n$$\nThus one may prescribe the valuation and $u$ bits of the odd unit of each input coefficient while keeping every *successor* state in its stated centred interval. The initial state is arbitrary.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.prop-2adic-nogo","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.prop-2adic-nogo","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.prop-2adic-nogo%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_centred_completion_of_fixed_precision%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.prop-2adic-nogo%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_centred_completion_of_fixed_precision%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_centred_completion_of_fixed_precision"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c